 "and_the_honest_caveat": "expected_NET_NEW for a country with no pages assumes its families behave like the captured average. The destination fan-out result on 2026-10-06 is the warning against trusting that: 292,613 raw rows produced 263,742 TRANSLATION_ONLY rejections, so a raw candidate count is not a page count. Every figure here is replaced by a measured one as the country is captured and run.",
 "a_correction_to_the_premise_this_file_was_asked_for": "The instruction was to materialise about 40 countries that had qualified demand and no pages. That was true of the 422,825-row manifest. It is NOT true of the 401,393-row one: the destination run put pages into 39 further countries, so 98 of the 99 qualified countries now have at least one page and only MC-adjacent single-page cases remain. The remaining gap is not DEMAND and it is not COUNTRY COVERAGE. It is CAPTURE DEPTH: 29 countries have full OSM layers and 69 have only the gazetteer, climate and Wikidata, which is why Singapore holds 18 pages, Luxembourg 17, Qatar 26 and Monaco 3.",
 "so_the_real_queue_is_under_captured_countries_not_missing_ones": {
