 "and_two_distinct_causes_which_need_different_work": "A country showing layers_missing of none and still far below its benchmark - BR at 32,082, MX 17,229, PH 14,604, BE 7,724, PT 5,746, MY 5,730 - is NOT waiting on a download. Its gap is the measured-tier cap and the per-market family gate, so capturing it again would add nothing. A country missing parents, places, poi, outdoor and trails - IN, UA, RO, CA, AR, ZA, CZ, TZ, FI, CL - is waiting on exactly that download. Only the second group is queued, and RO and TZ were added because they were in neither the queue nor the mirror-blocked list.",
 "what_the_benchmark_is_worth": "11.72 pages per gazetteer city is measured over the 29 captured countries, and it is dominated by the home markets with full family coverage, so it OVERSTATES a destination-only country. The destination fan-out result on the same day is the standing warning: 292,613 raw rows produced 263,742 TRANSLATION_ONLY rejections. Treat every expected figure here as an upper bound to be replaced by a count, never as a forecast."
